### Why this and not something fancier
A superior forecasting model, ML-based fair-value estimation, or full limit-order-book microstructure modeling would take far longer than a few days to build and validate safely, and bad forecasts directly lose money. Structural arbitrage (mutually-exclusive-sum violations, nested-market bound violations) is close to riskless and simple to code. Market making on top of a blended, cross-checked fair value captures spread with controlled inventory risk. This is buildable by one developer in days: order book client, a fair-value blender, an Avellaneda-Stoikov-lite quoting loop, and a small relations config file for the arbitrage checks.

