I would build **one strategy: cross-market fair-value + passive liquidity**, with the local order book used for execution and a small set of external prediction markets used as a fast-moving information source.

 The key idea is: **don't try to forecast elections yourself. Estimate the probability from the best available market consensus, then trade only when the executable price is sufficiently far from that estimate.** This is much more implementable in a few days than a political/news/NLP model.

