| Emergency threshold                |                   95% |
| Individual contract limit          |  0.5–1% bankroll risk |
| Correlated-group limit             |          ~5% bankroll |
| Gross event exposure limit         |                  ~25% |
| Fill toxicity observation window   |                 2 sec |
| Maximum toxicity widening          |              +3 ticks |

I would tune only about **six** things initially: maker edge, taker threshold, \(\lambda\), base size, individual inventory limit and toxicity penalty.

Don't create a 40-dimensional backtest optimisation problem.

